{"id":"neet-2026r-q068","pn":68,"y":"Re-NEET 2026 · 21 Jun","tp":"The d- and f-Block Elements","st":"Melting points of 3d metals","q":"Given below are two statements: One is labelled as Assertion A and the other is labelled as Reason R.\nAssertion A: Generally, 3d transition metals have high melting points.\nReason R: Involvement of 3d-electrons in addition to 4s-electrons in the interatomic metallic bonding.\nIn light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below:","o":["Both A and R are correct and R is NOT the correct explanation of A","A is correct but R is not correct.","A is not correct but R is correct","Both A and R are correct and R is the correct explanation of A"],"c":3,"s":"The melting points of 3d transition metals are generally high.\nThis is because a greater number of electrons from (n − 1)d, in addition to the ns electrons, take part in interatomic metallic bonding."},
{"id":"neet-2026r-q076","pn":76,"y":"Re-NEET 2026 · 21 Jun","tp":"The d- and f-Block Elements","st":"Lanthanoids electronic configuration","q":"The lanthanide ion having four unpaired electrons is\n(Given : Atomic numbers of Ce = 58, Nd = 60, Tb = 65 and Ho = 67)","o":["Ce³⁺","Tb³⁺","Ho³⁺","Nd³⁺"],"c":2,"s":"Write the outermost configuration of each ion.\nHo³⁺ is 4f¹⁰: three paired orbitals and four single electrons, so 4 unpaired electrons.\nNd³⁺ is 4f³: 3 unpaired electrons.\nCe³⁺ is 4f¹: 1 unpaired electron.\nTb³⁺ is 4f⁸: one paired orbital and six single electrons, so 6 unpaired electrons.\nSo Ho³⁺ has four unpaired electrons.","sfig":{"w":260,"h":172,"alt":"4f orbital box diagrams: Ho³⁺ 4f¹⁰ has three paired and four single boxes (4 unpaired electrons); Nd³⁺ 4f³ has 3 and Ce³⁺ 4f¹ has 1 unpaired electron; Tb³⁺ 4f⁸ has one paired and six single boxes (6 unpaired electrons).","d":[["t",10,30,"Ho³⁺ 4f¹⁰",""],["r",80,15,24,20,""],["t",92,30,"↑↓","m"],["r",104,15,24,20,""],["t",116,30,"↑↓","m"],["r",128,15,24,20,""],["t",140,30,"↑↓","m"],["r",152,15,24,20,""],["t",164,30,"↑","m"],["r",176,15,24,20,""],["t",188,30,"↑","m"],["r",200,15,24,20,""],["t",212,30,"↑","m"],["r",224,15,24,20,""],["t",236,30,"↑","m"],["t",164,52,"4 unpaired electrons","ms"],["t",10,82,"Nd³⁺ 4f³  3 unpaired electrons",""],["t",10,106,"Ce³⁺ 4f¹  1 unpaired electron",""],["t",10,140,"Tb³⁺ 4f⁸",""],["r",80,125,24,20,""],["t",92,140,"↑↓","m"],["r",104,125,24,20,""],["t",116,140,"↑","m"],["r",128,125,24,20,""],["t",140,140,"↑","m"],["r",152,125,24,20,""],["t",164,140,"↑","m"],["r",176,125,24,20,""],["t",188,140,"↑","m"],["r",200,125,24,20,""],["t",212,140,"↑","m"],["r",224,125,24,20,""],["t",236,140,"↑","m"],["t",164,162,"6 unpaired electrons","ms"]]}},
{"id":"neet-2025-q071","pn":71,"y":"NEET 2025","tp":"The d- and f-Block Elements","st":"Magnetic properties, unpaired electrons","q":"Given below are two statements :\nStatement I : Ferromagnetism is considered as an extreme form of paramagnetism.\nStatement II : The number of unpaired electrons in a Cr²⁺ ion (Z = 24) is the same as that of a Nd³⁺ ion (Z = 60).\nIn the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below :","o":["Both Statement I and Statement II are true","Both Statement I and Statement II are false","Statement I is true but Statement II is false","Statement I is false but Statement II is true"],"c":2,"s":"Substances attracted very strongly in an applied magnetic field are called ferromagnetic.\nIn fact, ferromagnetism is an extreme form of paramagnetism.\nHence Statement I is correct.\nCr²⁺ = 3d⁴4s⁰\nUnpaired electrons = 4\nNd³⁺ = 4f³ 6s⁰\nUnpaired electrons = 3\nHence Statement II is incorrect."}
